# GPD Pocket 4 touchscreen calibration. Installed to
# /etc/udev/rules.d/99-touchscreen-calibration.rules.
#
# ONLY INSTALL THIS IF TOUCH IS ACTUALLY WRONG. Test rotation without it first.
#
# Why it is conditional rather than part of the base install: on Wayland, KWin
# maps touch input onto its output and applies the output transform itself, so
# touch usually follows screen rotation with no help. Hyprland did NOT do that,
# which is why the old setup had to call
# `hyprctl keyword input:touchdevice:transform` alongside every display rotation
# (see the deleted auto-rotate.sh). Installing a calibration matrix on top of a
# compositor that already transforms touch double-applies it, and the symptom -
# touch offset or inverted in some orientations - looks exactly like the problem
# it was meant to fix.
#
# Decision procedure:
#   1. Apply the accelerometer matrix (61-sensor-local.hwdb) and reboot.
#   2. Rotate the device. If the display AND touch both follow, stop. Do not
#      install this file.
#   3. If the display rotates but touch does not follow, install this, reload
#      udev rules, and re-test each orientation.
#
# Device name confirmed on this machine 2026-08-16 from /proc/bus/input/devices;
# it matches what the ArchWiki GPD Pocket 4 page documents. The matrix value is
# the ArchWiki one and has NOT been verified here, because step 2 above may make
# it unnecessary.

ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="event[0-9]*", ATTRS{name}=="NVTK0603:00 0603:F001", ENV{LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX}="0 1 0 -1 0 1"
